  "interpretation": [
    "Jointly unfreezing all three already-fitted local Canaria candidates produced the lowest cluster NMSE to the original teacher in all 3 exploratory seeds.",
    "After re-freezing that cluster, a matched-budget single Canaria trained only on cluster outputs preserved most of the gain and was the best recursive-recompilation schedule in all 3 seeds.",
    "Direct recompilation from the original teacher remained better in NMSE, so recursive Canaria-to-Canaria recompilation is not lossless in C1.",
    "The frozen local cluster was easiest to imitate relative to itself but was a poor approximation to the original teacher; better joint adaptation increased the difficulty of imitating the cluster while substantially improving original-teacher fidelity.",
    "Freeze schedule therefore appears to control a fidelity-versus-recompilability tradeoff. Fresh confirmatory seeds are required before public claim use."
